usage: tokenguard.py [-h] [--root ROOT]
                     {run,inspect,slice,log,stats,doctor,hook,mcp,init} ...

Bound agent context while retaining command exit status and raw local
evidence. This is a presentation helper, not a sandbox, test oracle or token
accounting API. Only Python outlines use an AST. Other outlines are explicitly
heuristic. Commands inherit stdin and environment; combined file capture is
not a transparent TTY.

positional arguments:
  {run,inspect,slice,log,stats,doctor,hook,mcp,init}
    run                 Run an argv command, preserve exit status and log
                        bytes
    inspect             Show bounded declarations and source fingerprint
    slice               Read an exact source range
    log                 Replay a bounded range from a raw log
    stats               Report observed output bytes, not billing tokens
    doctor              Report local prerequisites without changing
                        configuration
    hook                Conservatively adapt Claude build/test commands
    mcp                 Serve bounded local tools over stdio MCP
    init                Preview or apply non-destructive workspace MCP entries

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --root ROOT
